MobileGlues: big RGBA textures, the game's icons, kept as ASTC 4x4, a quarter of the memory.

Prototype. Factorio keeps its icons uncompressed: an RGBA8 atlas 8192 wide and its mipmaps, made empty and filled from
memory, a sprite at a time anywhere, never drawn into (Xiaomi 12T, base game: 8192x2592 and 3 levels, 113 MB). A
texture 4096 wide or more, made empty with glTexImage2D, is kept as ASTC 4x4 from its first upload (the game also
makes a 4096x4096 RGBA texture it only draws into): each upload goes into an RGBA copy on storage beside the BC ones,
and the 4x4 blocks it touches are encoded again, from the upload itself where it covers whole blocks, else from the
copy, 64 rows at a time. Read back, a level is the copy; asked, it's the game's RGBA8. One a framebuffer takes after
all goes back to RGBA from its copy. MG_RGBA_ASTC=0 leaves them RGBA.
